SM75 large-M W4A8 without changing canonical W4A16 decode weights.

VLLM_TURING_PREFILL_INT8=mlp|all (default off) selects target projections,
excluding the MTP module and lm_head. At M >= 1024 a custom op transiently
repacks ONE matrix to the W4A8 layout, folding negative group-scale signs into
codes and quantizing scales to Marlin's uint16 representation. Marlin then
quantizes activations and uses INT8 MMA. Small-M execution is unchanged.

This is lossy: INT8 activation rounding and the flipped -8 endpoint's
saturation to -7 affect prefill state. It is NOT an exact optimization or a
blanket quality recommendation. Canonical weights and scales are never
mutated; no model-sized duplicate remains resident. The mode is included in
the compilation hash so a baseline graph cannot silently bypass it.

Requires prefill-memory-and-extend.patch for the preceding env registration
hunk; bounded KV staging is recommended to provide activation headroom.
Tests: python bench/test_turing_marlin.py
Measurements and quality gate: docs/turing-prefill.md.

